issues.problem:
Several manual features are silently absent rather than explicitly excluded:
- the H-UDI TAP pins (TCK / TMS / TDI / TDO / TRST). SDIR is set only through them, so the H-UDI reset and the H-UDI interrupt can never fire;
- STBCR.PHZ / PPU pin states in standby;
- the read value of the write-only SDMR2 / SDMR3;
- IFC ≠ ×1 in FRQCR, which is stated in passing in §2.1.

'hold_div = pfz' cannot be applied to v1_fpu as it stands, because the divider's pipeline-side bookkeeping is age-based and all of it sits under `!frz`:
- dv_age compared with the constants dv_w (12/11/25/24) and dv_busy_left (10/9/23/22);
- the steal at wlo-3;
- the pend_fe/rf/st/wr masks and fscr_busy;
- the direct FR write at dv_age==dv_w (v1_fpu.sv ~338-343, 433-445, 675-690).

If the ages freeze under mah while only v1_fdiv runs, FDIV; P4 read; FADD comes out at 17. ci3 measured 15.0.

If the ages run under mah, the equality dv_age==dv_w passes during the hold, and the quotient is either written while F1/F2/FS are held or never written.

SOC's one-line change therefore gives wrong timing or a lost result, and §4.5 claims the measured P2 value (24.1, between 20 'free' and 30 'frozen') without deriving it.

